{"Title":"Noah Fernandes mitochondrial disease awareness day","BillNumber":"S2782","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MJR0","Name":"Michael J. Rodrigues","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MJR0","ResponseDate":"2024-05-09T14:43:54.783"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MJR0","Name":"Michael J. Rodrigues","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MJR0","ResponseDate":"2024-05-09T14:43:54.7833333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2782/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Amendment","Pinslip":"Senate, May 13, 2024 - Text of the Senate amendment (Senator Rodrigues) to the House Bill to establish Noah Fernandes mitochondrial disease awareness day (House, No. 4240).","DocumentText":"\tChapter 6 of the General Laws is hereby amended by striking out section 15GGGGG, as appearing in the 2022 Official Edition, and inserting in place thereof the following section:-\r\n\tSection 15GGGGG. The governor shall annually issue a proclamation setting apart the third full week in September as Mitochondrial Disease Awareness Week and the Friday of said week as Noah Fernandes Mitochondrial Disease Awareness Day, in recognition of the number of residents of the commonwealth affected by mitochondrial diseases and the need for increased public awareness, research and support for victims and their families, and to show appreciation for the services being provided in the commonwealth to alleviate the financial and emotional stress of the disease for families with children who are affected by mitochondrial diseases and other developmental disabilities, and recommending that the week and the day be observed in an appropriate manner by the people.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}